<Article
  title="What the developer community did"
  description="Bitcoin Optech's coverage, the libngu and COLDCARD pull requests opened after the entropy incident, an independent commit-history reconstruction checked against the pinned clones, and attributed process and licensing observations."
  standfirst="Four public incident-response proposals are tracked. Their state moved through 1 August 2026: one stayed open, two were closed by their own authors, and the firmware companion became a draft waiting on a new upstream proposal. That upstream proposal was merged on 5 August 2026. A separate commit-history analysis is checked claim by claim below."
  depth="plain"
  kicker="Responses"
  next={{
    href: '/response/ai/',
    label: 'AI and discovery',
    note: 'What post-disclosure tests show, and why the original discovery method remains unknown.',
  }}
>
  <Answer>
    <p>
      Outside Coinkite's own repository, the community response was proposals
      rather than shipped change. Three pull requests against the upstream
      <code>libngu</code> library and one companion COLDCARD firmware pull
      request were all still open and unreviewed or unmerged in the captures
      checked on 1 August 2026. One has since moved: libngu #61 was merged
      upstream on 5 August 2026, and the library publishes no releases, so no
      proposal is present in a numbered release as of 6 August 2026. Bitcoin
      Optech carried the advisory to its technical readership, and an
      independent developer published a commit-history reconstruction whose
      assertions are graded one by one below. Nothing here changes what an owner
      should do; it records what the developer community proposed.
    </p>
  </Answer>

  <h2>The upstream guard in the 1 August capture</h2>

  <p>
    <a href="/how-it-broke/#the-fix">The COLDCARD hotfix</a> replaces the linked
    <code>rng_get()</code> implementation for the affected boards. It does not
    change <code>libngu</code>'s original <code>#ifndef
    MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_RNG</code> guard. An integrator can encounter the same
    condition if it defines that macro as <code>(0)</code> and links a software
    <code>rng_get()</code> fallback.
  </p>

  <p>
    Three pull requests were opened against <code>switck/libngu</code>, two on
    <strong>31 July 2026</strong> and one on <strong>1 August 2026</strong>.
  </p>

